@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# Bun migration
+
+Validated with Bun 1.4.4. Install with `bun install --frozen-lockfile`, then
+run `bun run typecheck` (or the preserved `bun run check` entry point) and
+`bun run build`. Open `public/index.html` after building.
+
+The build still bundles `src/main.tsx` for browsers as an IIFE at
+`public/app.js`. Preact remains pinned to 10.29.0; its automatic JSX runtime
+comes from the same package. TypeScript paths preserve the `@lib/` alias.
+The public HTML files and application source are unchanged.
+
+Strict checking now uses the pinned TypeScript compiler with browser libraries,
+instead of `deno check`; Deno globals are intentionally unavailable. Bundling
+uses Bun, so generated JavaScript and its size can differ while the visible
+`Hello Ada` result and missing-element error remain unchanged. No run, serve,
+or test tasks existed in the original project.
+
+Bun has no Deno permission sandbox. These commands only check and bundle the
+browser application, but tooling executes with the invoking user's permissions.
+Bun's environment/configuration loading and bundler resolution can differ from
+Deno's; the build does not explicitly enable environment-variable inlining.
+No formatter or linter replacement is included.
